      "writtenOn": "2024-02-14T08:33:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Understood, I think you are right that `JavaInfoProvider` might not be appropriate here.\n\nimo one of the advantages of keeping this language agnostic will manifest when we use this provider for rust and cc aconfig libraries. With the current schema, rust and cc will set a `CodegenInfo` provider that has a `srcJars` property even though srcJars is not relevant for those languages. (albeit it will be empty)\n\nnit: Do we need to call this property `SrcJars`? Can we replace them with a more generic property `Srcs` and use the same switch same statement logic in line 84 of `aconfig/codegen/aconfig_declarations_group.go`?\n\nDont mean this be blocking, but I was wondering how you anticipate this struct will evolve with cc and rust",
      "parentUuid": "a0299a56_9a831b3d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 31,
