      "writtenOn": "2024-02-14T18:23:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I understand your point, and agree that `srcs` would be generic and more applicable for all three codegen module types. However, the limitation of renaming the property to the generic `Srcs` somewhat coincides with the fact that `aconfig_declarations_group` can depend on one another, as explained in another comment. i.e. if we rename the property to the generic `Srcs`, we cannot differentiate the srcs provided from java, rust or cc modules when the provider is utilized in the `aconfig_declarations_group`. I think that one solution we could utilize is to introduce an separate provider for `aconfig_declarations_group`, which can specify srcs for each languages, while renaming the property as the generic srcs for this provider. WDYT?",
